  "text": "Mara says: “Yes. I’ll come over and read it once I’ve helped the passengers off.”\n\nThe whole story plays automatically with text. Pause whenever you need more time.\n\nA place where people make or present creative work, such as stories and pictures.\n\nPip, Sol and Grandma wait. Mara is still working, so nobody is telling her story.\n\nSol is still expecting the previous time. Tell him when the gathering will start.\n\nThis adventure used the earlier Sol sequence. Its original progress is preserved.\n\nPip crossed the river and planted the seed with Grandma. He had kept his promise.\n\nPip placed the memory of planting the seed with Grandma in their lantern-flower.\n\n“Grandma says you hardly visit. She thinks you don’t enjoy going there anymore.”\n\nAt the gathering · Listen to the whole telling, pause or read the complete text\n\nGrandma, Mara and Sol share a picnic. Four stones hold the tablecloth in place.\n\nThe roof tile is repaired and the flour is dry. Sol’s ending remains unwritten.\n\nPip offered to bring Mara a story if she is still working during the gathering.\n\nShare The Torn Wing with the people here before inviting Sol to tell his story.\n\nSol will share the version you chose, even if your working draft changed later.\n\nPip placed the memory of sharing stories in the garden in their lantern-flower.\n\nm289 34-5 10m-16-7-5 10m37 7-5 10m-18 4-5 10m-20-57-5 10M26 79l-5 10m13-41-5 10\n\nYour plan is bringing people to the garden. Continue their journey in the game.\n\nGrandma collects the seed at her landing and carries it to the planting place.\n\nMara finishes helping her passengers, comes to the garden and tells her story.\n\nPrepared ending from Sol’s account. Sol will share the version you last chose.\n\nM9 8a3 3 0 1 1 5 2c-2 1-2 2-2 4m0 3v.1M22 12a10 10 0 1 1-20 0 10 10 0 0 1 20 0",
